# 15. AUTHENTICATION AND SECURITY

Implement role-based access control.

Roles:

- super_admin
- employer
- candidate

Security requirements:

1. Enable RLS on every table containing application or user data.
2. Create policies based on authenticated user identity.
3. Candidates can access and update only their own records.
4. Employers can access only their own company and permitted applications.
5. Super Admin access must be securely restricted.
6. Never trust frontend role information.
7. Validate permissions on the server.
8. Never expose service_role keys.
9. Never expose Razorpay secrets.
10. Protect sensitive API routes.
11. Validate all user inputs.
12. Prevent SQL injection.
13. Prevent unauthorised data access.
14. Apply rate limits to sensitive endpoints.
15. Protect authentication and password reset workflows.

Do not create an insecure policy that allows all authenticated users to read all records.

Create and test RLS policies for every table.

Use server-side authorization for all privileged operations.

